        "exampleID": "prepared-embedding-classifier",
        "sourceResource": "embedding-observations",
        "title": "Explore Embedding in a categorical classifier",
        "subtitle": "Use category numbers to select rows from a learned table.",
        "disclosureTitle": "How category numbers become learned vectors",
        "formula": "An integer selects a row of numbers from a table. Those numbers are a vector: a short list the model can learn.",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Supply whole-number categories through Integer input. Each number must name a valid table row; no rounding of decimal values is performed.",
          "Embedding appends a vector direction to each selected category. Inspect the integer input and the output numbers after running the example.",
          "Padding suppresses learning changes to one chosen row; repeated categories can share accumulated changes. Maximum norm limits selected row lengths and may change even frozen table rows. On Apple GPU that norm adjustment uses the documented CPU fallback.",
          "The categorical example has its own data file and editable settings. The Embedding lab provides measured lookup, padding/frequency and forward weight-change exercises. Sparse learning with Adam is not supported."
        ],
        "buttonTitle": "Open categorical classifier example",
        "exampleSource": "Sources/KwipMLCore/WorkflowExamples.swift"
      }
